From: John Morkel <john@morkel.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:40:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: set the priority of the VLAN tags a PPE flow
 pushes

The vlan1 and vlan2 words of a FOE entry hold the TCI of the tags the
entry pushes: the vendor SDK writes there the whole TCI it parsed from
the frame, priority included. airoha_ppe writes the VLAN ID alone, so a
flow offloaded from a vlan push action that sets a priority leaves the
PPE with PCP 0, where the same flow on the CPU leaves with the priority
it asked for. On a PON uplink that priority is part of what the OLT
provisions, and it can select the GEM port of the flow.

Put each push's priority into its TCI. A push without a priority, such
as every one the netfilter flowtable offloads, keeps PCP 0.

Signed-off-by: John Morkel <john@morkel.me>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
index 99e9183..03d8eec 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -465,10 +465,14 @@ static int airoha_ppe_foe_entry_prepare(struct airoha_eth *eth,
 					    data->pppoe.sid);
 	}
 
+	/* vlan1 and vlan2 are the whole TCI of the pushed tags */
 	if (data->vlan.num) {
-		l2->vlan1 = data->vlan.hdr[0].id;
+		l2->vlan1 = data->vlan.hdr[0].id |
+			    FIELD_PREP(VLAN_PRIO_MASK, data->vlan.hdr[0].prio);
 		if (data->vlan.num == 2)
-			l2->vlan2 = data->vlan.hdr[1].id;
+			l2->vlan2 = data->vlan.hdr[1].id |
+				    FIELD_PREP(VLAN_PRIO_MASK,
+					       data->vlan.hdr[1].prio);
 	}
 
 	if (wlan_etype >= 0) {
